{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>A holy linen tunic.</b> Along with saying ״holy״ regarding the tunic, He did not suffice with what He concluded by saying ״they are holy garments.״ Perhaps it is because the verse was concerned lest a person reason in his mind that HaShem did not command making the garments of holiness but rather only the three garments other than the tunic, since the tunic is a garment that every person is obligated to wear and would be his own, and regarding the three it is that He said ״holy garments״ — for they are garments that can befit the honor of the ministers on high. Therefore He said <b>a linen tunic</b> etc. — that it too is holy. And so that you not think that specifically the tunic HaShem decreed should be of holiness, therefore He went back and said <b>they are holy garments</b> — all of them together." "Further it appears possible to say that He intends to say two things: the first, that the linen from which they make the tunic should be of holiness, and the same applies to the rest of the garments; and the verse informed us of this ruling in the first instance. The second matter is that also the making of the garments should be of holiness, which is what He concluded by saying <b>they are holy garments</b>." "<b>Further</b> it appears that in saying <b>they are holy garments</b> He intends that the matter not appear outside the realm of proper conduct — for a servant of the King, who is the priest whom HaShem adorned and honored with garments of glory, as it is written (Exodus 28:2) ״for honor and for splendor,״ and at the time he is elevated to so great a service, He says to him: remove your adornment from upon yourself — therefore He said <b>they are holy garments</b>, meaning, garments fit for holiness they are, and no others. And the reason is that those glorified garments contain things within them, as our Sages of blessed memory said (Leviticus Rabbah 21; Rosh HaShanah 26a): a prosecutor does not become a defender." "Or it may hint at the reason of (Proverbs 25:6) ״do not glorify yourself before a king״ — our Master, blessed be He, is holy and awesome is His name — and He said <b>they are holy garments</b>, meaning, that with them it is fitting to serve in the holy of holies where the Name of Elohim dwells. And our Sages of blessed memory said: ״holy shall he don״ — that they should be of holiness, meaning, all four are learned from the tunic, that they should be of holiness; and He went back to say <b>they are holy garments</b> — they expounded, of blessed memory (Torat Kohanim), that this comes to teach concerning all priestly garments that they should be of holiness. And these and those are the words of the living Elohim."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:57:35.527786480Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}